-- WHY 6.9.0 STILL DID NOT HAND OUT FOOD (decompiled this session, 2026-10-31):
--
-- Serve is not a remote. It cannot be. Two decompiled modules prove it:
--
-- 1. Source.Systems.Restaurant.GrabFood.AttemptGrab(tycoon, foodModel):
--        local ok, info = Events.Restaurant.GrabFood:InvokeServer(foodModel)
--        Storage[#+1] = { Model = foodModel, FoodKey = foodModel.Name, Tycoon = tycoon,
--                         TargetPlayerName = info.TargetPlayerName,
--                         TargetCarId = info.TargetCarId, KidFlag = info.KidFlag }
--    The tray contents and the TARGET come from the server's InvokeServer return, and
--    GrabFood:IsHoldingFoodForNPC(order, kidFlag) only accepts an entry whose FoodKey ==
--    the customer's order. There is no client function that serves from a payload we build,
--    so TaskCompleted 'Serve' was never a serve call - the server ignored it. That is the
--    whole reason 6.9.0 picked up fine and handed out nothing.
